Switch the template's publish workflow from a project token to the repository's link.

For LordBaryhobal/yukibana-template-scala, against .github/workflows/publish.yml
as it is there now (on push of tags v*, actions/checkout@v4, then
tothambrus11/yukibana-cloud/action@main with url, project, token and label).
Apply it from that repository's root with

    git apply github-template.patch

(or `patch -p1 < github-template.patch`, which tolerates a line that moved).
Everything above the first "---" line is description, which both ignore.

What it changes, and why (docs/cloud/github.md in Yukibana-Ed/Yukibana):

* The Action is Yukibana-Ed/Yukibana/action@main, where it lives since the
  cloud moved into the Yukibana repository; tothambrus11/yukibana-cloud is the
  old one.
* `project` and `token` are gone. With neither, the Action runs
  `yukibana publish --ci`: the job asks GitHub for an OIDC token, the registry
  checks that this repository is linked to a project, and the release goes to
  every project linked to it that `projects` names. A link is made on the
  project page and the repository cannot remove it, so `projects` is the
  repository's say in where its hidden tests go. It reads the
  YUKIBANA_PROJECT variable repositories made from the template already
  have, so a repository made from it needs no secret, that one variable and
  a link on the project page; the `projectId` a template's yukibana.json may
  carry is ignored.
* `permissions: id-token: write` lets the job ask for that token, and
  `contents: read` keeps checkout working once a permissions block exists
  (any permission not named becomes none).
* The tag filter stays `v*`. The registry publishes by link only from tags;
  the filter only chooses which tags.

Once merged, the YUKIBANA_TOKEN secret of the template (and of repositories
made from it) is unused and can be deleted; the YUKIBANA_PROJECT variable
stays, and may list several project ids, separated by commas.
Repositories already made from the template keep the old workflow until the
same change is made in them; with their secret and variable still set, the
old workflow keeps publishing with the token until then, for as long as the
old Action stays where it is.

The registry's GITHUB_TEMPLATE can name this template once this is merged
(docs/cloud/deploy.md, step 8).

--- a/.github/workflows/publish.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/publish.yml
@@ -5,14 +5,20 @@
     tags:
       - 'v*'
 
+# Publishes to the projects linked to this repository on their Yukibana
+# project page (Releases, Repository) that the YUKIBANA_PROJECT variable
+# names, with GitHub's OIDC token: no secret to set. Only tags publish.
+permissions:
+  contents: read
+  id-token: write
+
 jobs:
   publish:
     runs-on: ubuntu-latest
     steps:
       - uses: actions/checkout@v4
-      - uses: tothambrus11/yukibana-cloud/action@main
+      - uses: Yukibana-Ed/Yukibana/action@main
         with:
           url: https://cloud.yukibana.dev
-          project: ${{ vars.YUKIBANA_PROJECT }}
-          token: ${{ secrets.YUKIBANA_TOKEN }}
+          projects: ${{ vars.YUKIBANA_PROJECT }}
           label: ${{ github.ref_name }}
